            <ArticleTitle>CT Imaging Findings of Metastatic Spindle Cell Sarcoma of Prostate: A Case Report and Review of the Literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>145-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5152/eurasianjmed.2014.43</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sarcomas of the prostate are rare tumors. Imaging plays an important role in the management and diagnosis of patients with prostate sarcomas. Their clinic-pathologic features are well described, but the imaging features of these tumors have rarely been documented in the literature and have appeared mainly as case reports. Herein, we present a rare case of metastatic spindle cell sarcoma of prostate with computed tomography imaging findings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
